  {
    "hotel_id": "652131",
    "hotel_url": "https://www.agoda.com/ibis-styles-krabi-ao-nang/hotel/krabi-th.html",
    "name": "ibis Styles Krabi Ao Nang",
    "detail": "We were very pleased with our stay at the Ibis Syles, a brand new hotel in the Ao Nang area of Krabi. The hotel is so new that everything is still bright and squeeky clean. There was a lovely, large pool, with for once a hotel with enough poolside seating to go around. More then ample even at the peak times. The hotel is very close to the main road down into Ao Nang, with many restaurants, spas and tour agents within a 5 - 10 minute walk. The beach itself is a bit further away, I'd say about 15 - 20 minutes depending on how fast you want to walk. The hotel does provide regular hourly transportation down to the beach during the day, though you are expected to find your own way back to the hotel. The decor of the hotel is very bright and colorful, and I found it quite refreshing. The rooms are not big, which is a shame they do feel a bit cramped, but they were spotless, and everyone had a balcony. Ours overlooked the pool. The only real disappointment was the breakfast buffet, which I found not up to standard at all. The eggs were stone cold, the sausages were drowning in tepid water, and I have never seen greasier bacon anywhere. The coffee was possibly the worst I have had at a hotel in Thailand in the past three years, tasting bitter and burnt. Also, the selection of Thai food was surprisingly sparse and limited. The whole breakfast presentation needs to be re-examined. Otherwise, this was a very nice hotel, and we really enjoyed our time there. In spite of the low quality of the breakfast, we would not hesitate to go back next time we are in Krabi. ",
